.TH MKPASS 1 "October 2026" "mkpass 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mkpass \- stateless deterministic password and passphrase generator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkpass
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B mkpass
\fBconfig\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.br
.B mkpass
\fBupdate\fR [\fIUPDATE_OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkpass
is a stateless, deterministic password and passphrase generator. Instead of storing generated secret passwords in an encrypted vault,
.B mkpass
derives strong passwords on-demand using a single \fBMaster Password\fR and a public \fBService Name\fR (such as "github.com" or "email").
.PP
Every time you enter the same Master Password, Service Name, and parameters (such as length or character sets),
.B mkpass
computes the exact same password using cryptographic key derivation functions (Argon2id or HMAC-SHA512).
.PP
Non-secret configuration parameters (algorithm choice, length, character sets, separators, patterns, comments) are stored in a local SQLite database (\fB~/.config/mkpass/config.db\fR) to provide auto-completion suggestions and remember per-service preferences. Persistent global defaults and update settings are maintained in a user configuration file (\fB~/.config/mkpass/mkpass.conf\fR). Even without access to the local database or config file, knowing your Master Password and configuration parameters guarantees password regeneration on any device.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-password\fR \fIPASSWORD\fR
Specify the Master Password. If omitted in interactive mode, the user will be securely prompted. Can also be set via the \fBMKPASS_PASSWORD\fR environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-service\fR \fISERVICE\fR
Specify the target Service Name (e.g., "github.com"). Supports auto-completion in interactive mode. Can also be set via the \fBMKPASS_SERVICE\fR environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-comment\fR \fICOMMENT\fR
Specify a descriptive comment or metadata for the service (e.g., "Work account - MFA recovery"). Stored in the local database. Can also be set via the \fBMKPASS_COMMENT\fR environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-algorithm\fR \fIALGO\fR
Specify the generation algorithm. Accepts numeric IDs (1-5) or descriptive strings:
.RS
.IP "1, password/argon2" 4
Password using \fBArgon2id\fR key derivation (Recommended modern default).
.IP "2, password/sha512" 4
Password using \fBHMAC-SHA512\fR iterative hashing.
.IP "3" 4
Legacy algorithm support (requires \fBenable_old_algorithm = true\fR in configuration).
.IP "4, passphrase/diceware" 4
Passphrase using \fBDiceware EFF Large\fR wordlist.
.IP "5, passphrase/wordnet" 4
Passphrase using \fBWordNet Pattern\fR grammatical structure.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-char\-classes\fR \fICLASSES\fR
Specify character classes to include for password generation. Accepts numeric strings (e.g. \fB1234\fR) or comma-separated names (e.g. \fBlowercase,uppercase,digits,symbols\fR):
.RS
.IP "1, lowercase" 4
Lower-case letters (a-z)
.IP "2, uppercase" 4
Upper-case letters (A-Z)
.IP "3, digits" 4
Digits (0-9)
.IP "4, symbols" 4
Special symbols (!@#$%^&*...)
.IP "5, custom" 4
Custom character set (specified via \fB\-\-custom\-chars\fR)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-custom\-chars\fR \fICHARS\fR
Specify custom characters to append to the generation pool when character class 5 is selected. Can also be set via the \fBMKPASS_CUSTOM_CHARS\fR environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-length\fR \fILEN\fR
Set derived password or passphrase length (number of characters or words depending on algorithm). Range: 1 to 128. Default: 16. Can also be set via the \fBMKPASS_LENGTH\fR environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-\-separator\fR \fISEPARATOR\fR
Set word separator string for passphrases (e.g., "-", " ", "/"). Can also be set via the \fBMKPASS_SEPARATOR\fR environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-\-pattern\fR \fIPATTERN\fR
Set grammatical passphrase structure for WordNet pattern algorithm (e.g., "adj,noun,verb"). Can also be set via the \fBMKPASS_PASSPHRASE_PATTERN\fR environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-\-digits\fR \fIy|n\fR
Enable or disable inclusion of random digits in generated passphrases. Can also be set via the \fBMKPASS_DIGITS\fR environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-\-symbols\fR \fIy|n\fR
Enable or disable inclusion of random symbols in generated passphrases. Can also be set via the \fBMKPASS_SYMBOLS\fR environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-\-substitutions\fR \fIy|n\fR
Allow or disallow leetspeak-style character substitutions in passphrases (e.g., 'a' -> '4'). Can also be set via the \fBMKPASS_SUBSTITUTIONS\fR environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-\-capitalize\fR \fIy|n\fR
Enable or disable word capitalization in passphrases. Can also be set via the \fBMKPASS_CAPITALIZE\fR environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-qr\-code\fR
Render the generated password directly in the terminal as a UTF-8 / ASCII QR code instead of plain text.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-infinite\fR
Run in a continuous interactive prompt loop until interrupted (Ctrl+C).
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-defaults\fR
Automatically accept saved default settings from the local database. Repeat flag (\fB\-dd\fR) to bypass all non-essential interactive prompts.
.TP
\fB\-D\fR, \fB\-\-delete\fR
Enter record deletion mode to remove stored service configurations from the local database.
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-info\fR
Enter record info mode to display full service configuration from the local database.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display command summary and exit.

.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS config
Manage persistent user configuration settings stored in \fB~/.config/mkpass/mkpass.conf\fR.
.TP
\fBmkpass config get\fR \fIKEY\fR
Display the current configured value for the specified configuration key.
.TP
\fBmkpass config set\fR \fIKEY\fR \fIVALUE\fR
Set and persist a configuration option in \fBmkpass.conf\fR.
.TP
\fBmkpass config unset\fR \fIKEY\fR
Remove the specified option from \fBmkpass.conf\fR, reverting it to its built-in default.
.TP
\fBmkpass config print\fR [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-all\fR]
Print active configuration settings. If \fB\-a\fR or \fB\-\-all\fR is specified, all settings including defaults are displayed.

.PP
Valid configuration keys:
.RS
.IP "\fBcheck_updates\fR" 4
Boolean (\fBtrue\fR/\fBfalse\fR). Enable or disable periodic background checks for software updates. (Default: \fBtrue\fR)
.IP "\fBupdate_check_interval_days\fR" 4
Integer (1-365). Number of days between periodic update checks. (Default: \fB7\fR)
.IP "\fBupdate_channel\fR" 4
String (\fB"stable"\fR or \fB"prerelease"\fR). Release channel to query. (Default: \fB"stable"\fR)
.IP "\fBalgorithm\fR" 4
Default algorithm (\fBpassword/argon2\fR, \fBpassword/sha512\fR, \fBpassphrase/diceware\fR, \fBpassphrase/wordnet\fR).
.IP "\fBlength\fR" 4
Default password length or passphrase word count.
.IP "\fBchar_classes\fR" 4
Default character classes (e.g. \fB1234\fR or \fBlowercase,uppercase,digits,symbols\fR).
.IP "\fBcustom_chars\fR" 4
Default custom characters.
.IP "\fBseparator\fR" 4
Default passphrase separator string.
.IP "\fBpassphrase_pattern\fR" 4
Default WordNet passphrase grammatical pattern.
.IP "\fBdigits\fR" 4
Boolean. Default digits inclusion for passphrases.
.IP "\fBsymbols\fR" 4
Boolean. Default symbols inclusion for passphrases.
.IP "\fBsubstitutions\fR" 4
Boolean. Default leetspeak substitution flag for passphrases.
.IP "\fBcapitalize\fR" 4
Boolean. Default word capitalization flag for passphrases.
.IP "\fBenable_old_algorithm\fR" 4
Boolean. Enable deprecated legacy algorithm 3. (Default: \fBfalse\fR)
.RE

.SS update
Check GitHub Releases for new versions of \fBmkpass\fR and install updates with SHA-512 cryptographic verification.
.TP
\fB\-\-check\-only\fR
Check whether a new release is available and display release notes, without downloading or installing.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Automatically proceed with download, checksum verification, and installation without prompting for confirmation.

.SH PASSIVE UPDATE NOTIFICATIONS
When update checking is enabled (\fBcheck_updates = true\fR), \fBmkpass\fR consults cached release metadata (\fB~/.cache/mkpass/update_state.json\fR) during standard password generation. If a newer release is known to exist, a single-line advisory is emitted to \fBstderr\fR:
.PP
.RS
\fI[mkpass] Update available: vX.Y.Z (current: vA.B.C). Run 'mkpass update' to install.\fR
.RE
.PP
This notification is automatically suppressed when \fBstderr\fR is redirected or piped, and is never shown when \fBcheck_updates\fR is set to \fBfalse\fR.

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B MKPASS_PASSWORD
Master Password to use for generation.
.TP
.B MKPASS_SERVICE
Target Service Name.
.TP
.B MKPASS_COMMENT
Service description or comment metadata.
.TP
.B MKPASS_ALGORITHM
Default algorithm identifier (e.g. "password/argon2" or 1-5).
.TP
.B MKPASS_CHAR_CLASSES
Character classes string.
.TP
.B MKPASS_CUSTOM_CHARS
Custom character set.
.TP
.B MKPASS_LENGTH
Password length.
.TP
.B MKPASS_SEPARATOR
Passphrase word separator.
.TP
.B MKPASS_PASSPHRASE_PATTERN
WordNet passphrase pattern.
.TP
.B MKPASS_DIGITS
Include digits flag (y/n).
.TP
.B MKPASS_SYMBOLS
Include symbols flag (y/n).
.TP
.B MKPASS_SUBSTITUTIONS
Allow substitutions flag (y/n).
.TP
.B MKPASS_CAPITALIZE
Capitalize words flag (y/n).

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mkpass/config.db
SQLite database storing local non-secret service configuration entries, comments, and options history.
.TP
.I ~/.config/mkpass/mkpass.conf
TOML user configuration file containing persistent defaults and update preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/mkpass/update_state.json
Local cache storing update check timestamps, HTTP ETags, and latest known release information.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Interactive execution:
$ mkpass
.TP
.B Generate password for github.com non-interactively using defaults:
$ MKPASS_PASSWORD="my_master_secret" mkpass \-s github.com \-d \-d
.TP
.B Generate password with comment attached:
$ mkpass \-s aws.amazon.com \-m "Root production access"
.TP
.B Generate password as a terminal QR code:
$ mkpass \-s email \-q
.TP
.B Display full service record from local database:
$ mkpass \-I \-s github.com
.TP
.B Delete a saved service entry from local database:
$ mkpass \-D \-s oldservice.com
.TP
.B Check if a newer version of mkpass is available:
$ mkpass update \-\-check\-only
.TP
.B Download and install latest release:
$ mkpass update
.TP
.B Disable periodic automatic update checking:
$ mkpass config set check_updates false
.TP
.B View all current configuration settings:
$ mkpass config print \-a

